<rml>
<head>
    <title>Card</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="menu.rcss"/>
</head>
<body class="cut">
<!-- A card of text over a picture of the game: two lines in the lower third of the
     window. It has no buttons. The game writes the two lines and sets, in every frame,
     how much of three things is there (ui::UiLayer::setOpacity): the black over the
     picture, the card itself and the hint. The intro shows its five cards with it
     (game/Intro.hpp), and any other text between two screens can use it too. -->
<div class="black" id="black"></div>
<div class="story" id="card">
    <div class="story-band"></div>
    <div class="story-lines">
        <div class="story-mark"></div>
        <p class="story-line" id="line-first"></p>
        <p class="story-line second" id="line-second"></p>
    </div>
</div>
<p class="keys corner" id="hint">Press any key to skip</p>
</body>
</rml>
